= Modal logic — Simple =

'''Modal logic''' is logic for ideas such as possibility and necessity.

Two common symbols are:

<pre>
□P = P is necessary
◇P = P is possible
</pre>

Modal logic can also be adapted to talk about knowledge, belief, time, or obligation.

One common method imagines different possible worlds or states and asks which ones are accessible from the current one.

Something necessary is true in every relevant accessible world.

Something possible is true in at least one.

Necessary does not mean “very probable”. Probability and modality are different ideas.

